.TH WERKMEISTER-FEATURE-OPEN 1 "" "werkmeister" "Werkmeister Manual"
.SH NAME
werkmeister\-feature\-open \- Open a feature\-tagged Chrome window with the X\-Feature cookie set (no Playwright)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwerkmeister feature open\fR [feature]
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-url <url>\fR
Full start URL (overrides \-\-path). Default: the first routed host's homepage.
.TP
\fB\-\-path <path>\fR
Path appended to the first routed host (default: test_path from .werkmeister/workspace.yml, else TEST_PATH from .env, else '/').
.TP
\fB\-\-size <W,H>\fR
Window size WIDTH,HEIGHT (default: 1440,900).
.TP
\fB\-\-position <X,Y>\fR
Window position X,Y (default: staggered by feature name).
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Launches an isolated Chrome window for a feature: it sets the \fBX\-Feature\fR routing cookie and tags the window (title prefix and corner badge) so it is plainly that feature's window. It drives Chrome over the DevTools Protocol, without Playwright.
.PP
Routing only resolves while the feature is running (\fBwerkmeister feature up\fR). Otherwise the cookie is set but traffic falls through to the k8s baseline.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
werkmeister feature open my\-feature
werkmeister feature open my\-feature \-\-path /settings
werkmeister feature open my\-feature \-\-size 1280,800 \-\-position 0,0
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBwerkmeister\fR(1)
